  "narrative": "I assessed the twelve newly delivered results against direction-specific signed effects and approximate 10% clinical scales: SMARCA2 about 0.042, WRN about 0.030, USP7 and NFE2L2 about 0.009, KIF18A about 0.026, EGFR/KRAS about 0.024 to 0.025. For direction -1, positive signed means stronger dependency; for direction +1, positive signed means weaker dependency. H60, H61, H62, H63, H64, H66, and H67 all show extremely large, direction-consistent estimates far above their outcome thresholds with 95% Welch intervals also far above threshold. Specifically, SMARCA4 loss remains associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency in KEAP1-intact and KRAS-wildtype contexts; TP53 loss remains associated with weaker USP7 dependency in KEAP1-intact context; KEAP1 loss remains associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency in STK11-intact and KRAS-wildtype contexts; and MSI-high remains associated with stronger WRN dependency in KEAP1-intact and STK11-intact contexts. I accept these as dataset-specific context associations, not causal or generalizable claims. They strengthen the internal robustness of the four accepted signals and make simple confounding by KEAP1, KRAS, STK11, TP53, library, batch, or ARID1A less plausible for the tested comparisons. H68 is informative for specificity but not decisive: MSI-high versus KIF18A is near null at signed -0.0027, interval -0.0387 to +0.0334, and although the point estimate does not support broader MSI-high-associated stronger KIF18A dependency, the upper interval bound still allows a clinically meaningful positive effect, so I leave it unresolved and deferred. H72 is not decisive for ERBB2-amplification-associated weaker EGFR dependency: signed +0.0032, interval -0.0231 to +0.0296; the point is near null but the interval allows a clinically meaningful weaker effect, so unresolved and deferred. H73 rejects the registered PTEN-loss-associated weaker EGFR-dependency claim because the signed estimate is -0.0059 and the interval upper bound +0.0171 lies below the approximate EGFR clinical threshold. This is evidence against clinically meaningful weaker EGFR dependency in PTEN-loss samples, although the slight negative direction and lower interval bound raise a possible but imprecise opposite effect that is not accepted here. H75 is a borderline new mechanistic test: NF1 loss versus weaker KRAS dependency gives signed +0.0202, interval -0.0086 to +0.0491. The point is below the KRAS threshold, but the interval allows a clinically meaningful positive effect; I leave it unresolved and active, but before validation I would prefer KRAS-mutation stratification because the overall test mixes KRAS-mutant and KRAS-wildtype biology. H80 is a technical control: matched RNA/DNA omics versus SMARCA2 dependency is near null at signed +0.0078, interval -0.0334 to +0.0491; this reduces but does not eliminate concern about data-processing stratum artifacts because the interval upper bound slightly exceeds the SMARCA2 threshold. I do not request validation now. The accepted context effects are already extraordinarily large and multiply internally replicated, while the new borderline driver effects are either not precise enough or need subgroup stratification before independent validation would be most informative.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 4 appraise update. New co-context results strengthen the four accepted dataset-specific associations. Accepted context associations: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 overall plus ARID1A-intact, batch_a, non-Avana, TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact, KRAS-wildtype; MSI-high -> stronger WRN overall plus Avana, BRCA2-intact, TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact, STK11-intact; KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 overall plus non-Avana, TP53-intact, STK11-intact, KRAS-wildtype; TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 overall plus non-Avana, SMARCA4-intact, KEAP1-intact. All remain association-only, not causal or generalizable therapeutic claims. H68 MSI-high vs KIF18A is near null but interval upper bound allows clinically meaningful positive effect, so unresolved/deferred. H72 ERBB2 amp vs EGFR weaker dependency is near null but interval allows meaningful positive, unresolved/deferred. H73 PTEN loss vs EGFR weaker dependency rejected because signed upper bound is below EGFR clinical threshold; possible opposite EGFR effect remains imprecise and not accepted. H75 NF1 loss vs KRAS weaker dependency is borderline, unresolved active, but KRAS stratification should come before validation. H80 matched omics control is near null but interval slightly allows meaningful SMARCA2 association, unresolved/deferred. No validation requested because accepted contexts are decisive and new borderline driver/control tests need sharper stratification or are not precise enough. Next analyze priorities: finish accepted-signal context completion: H16 SMARCA2/SMARCA4 Avana, H39 batch_b, H21 ARID1A interaction, H31 ARID1A loss in SMARCA4-intact, H35 USP7/TP53 Avana, H36 batch_a, H42 batch_b, H37 KRAS-wildtype, H65 NFE2L2/KEAP1 batch_a, H40 WRN/MSI batch_b, H47 KIF18A/TP53 non-Avana, H22 KEAP1/STK11 interaction. Driver priorities: H74 ERBB2 amp EGFR KRAS-wildtype, H76 PIK3CA KRAS-wildtype KRAS, H43 EGFR amp adenocarcinoma KRAS-wildtype, H77 ERBB2 amp adenocarcinoma, H45 KRAS mutation excluding BRAF V600E, H23 KRAS adenocarcinoma, H29 KRAS STK11-intact. Specificity/controls: H69 MSI POLR2A, H70/H71 MYC KIF18A/POLR2A, H78 marker E WRN, H79 marker F USP7, H81 matched omics WRN. Validation reserve for decisive borderline driver claim after subgroup context or for a newly precise clinically meaningful result, potentially H3/H75/H74/H76/H43/H45 depending on results."
